{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-31078","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-40898","text":"TRAAVIIS — Architecture & the road to the environment surface"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40899","marks":["bold"],"text":"Thesis."},{"id":"spn-40900","text":" TRAAVIIS is the local-first toolchain for "},{"id":"spn-40901","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade agent evaluation"},{"id":"spn-40902","text":". Not another coding agent, not a model router, not an RL cloud, not the whole TRVM research workbench. Its core loop is: "},{"id":"spn-40903","marks":["italic"],"text":"freeze the subject → run the evaluation → score explicit evidence → verify → preserve a re-verifiable receipt."},{"id":"spn-40904","text":" TRVM supplies the strongest exact-replay substrate under it; Evidence Residency is its first repository-evidence substrate.  "},{"id":"spn-40905","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write the wall. Run the world. Keep the proof."}]}],"id":"blk-31079","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-31081","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40906","text":"This document describes the product boundary, what ships today, and the road to the environment surface ("},{"id":"spn-40907","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-40908","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-40909","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-40910","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-40911","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-40912","text":"). It supersedes the earlier \"terminal harness engineer\" thesis — that positioning is retired."}]},{"id":"blk-31082","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-40913","text":"1. The product boundary"}]},{"id":"blk-31083","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40914","text":"The seams are frozen on purpose. "},{"id":"spn-40915","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-40916","text":" carries "},{"id":"spn-40917","marks":["bold"],"text":"no substrate semantics"},{"id":"spn-40918","text":"; it packages capabilities the layers below already provide, for someone who does not know the internal history of TRVM."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-31085","spans":[{"id":"spn-40919","text":"layer"}]},{"id":"blk-31086","spans":[{"id":"spn-40920","text":"responsibility"}]}],"id":"blk-31084","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-31087","spans":[{"id":"spn-40921","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS"}]},{"id":"blk-31088","spans":[{"id":"spn-40922","text":"the product — CLI, environment SDK, evaluator, packaging, visual workbench"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31089","spans":[{"id":"spn-40923","marks":["bold"],"text":"trvs"}]},{"id":"blk-31090","spans":[{"id":"spn-40924","text":"the command-line interface"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31091","spans":[{"id":"spn-40925","marks":["bold"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-31092","spans":[{"id":"spn-40926","text":"the substrate-neutral assignment and evaluation contract"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31093","spans":[{"id":"spn-40927","marks":["bold"],"text":"WallRiderLang"}]},{"id":"blk-31094","spans":[{"id":"spn-40928","text":"the language for TRVM worlds, actors and world rules"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31095","spans":[{"id":"spn-40929","marks":["bold"],"text":"Forge"}]},{"id":"blk-31096","spans":[{"id":"spn-40930","text":"the compiler, identity and artifact pipeline"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31097","spans":[{"id":"spn-40931","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM"}]},{"id":"blk-31098","spans":[{"id":"spn-40932","text":"the deterministic execution substrate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31099","spans":[{"id":"spn-40933","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spinner Bench"}]},{"id":"blk-31100","spans":[{"id":"spn-40934","text":"the reference workbench and conformance laboratory"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-31101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40935","text":"Two rules follow directly:"}]},{"id":"blk-31102","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31104","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40936","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spinner Bench is not TRAAVIIS."},{"id":"spn-40937","text":" It remains the place where the"}]}],"id":"blk-31103","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-31105","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40938","text":"language/runtime is exercised, visually inspected, and proven. TRAAVIIS "},{"id":"spn-40939","marks":["italic"],"text":"consumes"},{"id":"spn-40940","text":" those capabilities and packages them."}]},{"id":"blk-31106","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31108","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40941","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvs` invents no state semantics."},{"id":"spn-40942","text":" Every command is a thin call over the"}]}],"id":"blk-31107","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-31109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40943","text":"Forge engine's stable public API ("},{"id":"spn-40944","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.engine → forge_api"},{"id":"spn-40945","text":"). Identity, lowering, folding, and verification live below the CLI and are versioned there."}]},{"id":"blk-31110","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-40946","text":"2. What is real today"}]},{"id":"blk-31111","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40947","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis"},{"id":"spn-40948","text":" is a zero-dependency Python package exposing the "},{"id":"spn-40949","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-40950","text":" command over "},{"id":"spn-40951","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.engine"},{"id":"spn-40952","text":". Seven commands fold real worlds:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-31113","spans":[{"id":"spn-40953","text":"command"}]},{"id":"blk-31114","spans":[{"id":"spn-40954","text":"contract"}]}],"id":"blk-31112","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-31115","spans":[{"id":"spn-40955","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs doctor"}]},{"id":"blk-31116","spans":[{"id":"spn-40956","text":"reports engine dir, API version, "},{"id":"spn-40957","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-40958","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-40959","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-40960","text":"/oracle status"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31117","spans":[{"id":"spn-40961","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs id"}]},{"id":"blk-31118","spans":[{"id":"spn-40962","text":"re-lowers source → "},{"id":"spn-40963","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-40964","text":" (pure identity)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31119","spans":[{"id":"spn-40965","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs inspect"}]},{"id":"blk-31120","spans":[{"id":"spn-40966","text":"lowered actors, edges, resolved static config, diagnostics"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31121","spans":[{"id":"spn-40967","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs run"}]},{"id":"blk-31122","spans":[{"id":"spn-40968","text":"folds the world through "},{"id":"spn-40969","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-40970","text":"; prints the per-epoch film"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31123","spans":[{"id":"spn-40971","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify"}]},{"id":"blk-31124","spans":[{"id":"spn-40972","text":"cross-checks "},{"id":"spn-40973","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-40974","text":" vs native "},{"id":"spn-40975","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-40976","text":" vs the Fixture oracle"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31125","spans":[{"id":"spn-40977","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs replay"}]},{"id":"blk-31126","spans":[{"id":"spn-40978","text":"re-folds and asserts a pinned "},{"id":"spn-40979","marks":["code"],"text":"--expect"},{"id":"spn-40980","text":" id / "},{"id":"spn-40981","marks":["code"],"text":"--film"},{"id":"spn-40982","text":" hash"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31127","spans":[{"id":"spn-40983","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs diff"}]},{"id":"blk-31128","spans":[{"id":"spn-40984","text":"folds two worlds and marks the first divergent epoch"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-31129","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40985","marks":["bold"],"text":"Identity model."},{"id":"spn-40986","text":" Presentation (position, colour, wire curve) never enters the hash; a rotor value or a rewire does. Run inputs (the scenario) are deliberately kept "},{"id":"spn-40987","marks":["italic"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-40988","text":" of the "},{"id":"spn-40989","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-40990","text":" and carried as a separate "},{"id":"spn-40991","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-40992","text":" digest. This is the split that makes an environment content-addressable."}]},{"id":"blk-31130","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-40993","marks":["bold"],"text":"Verification contract."},{"id":"spn-40994","text":" A film is not asserted — it is "},{"id":"spn-40995","marks":["italic"],"text":"checked by every applicable verifier"},{"id":"spn-40996","text":". The reference reducer ("},{"id":"spn-40997","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-40998","text":"), the compiled native reducer ("},{"id":"spn-40999","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-41000","text":"), and an independent oracle each run where their domain applies and must agree byte-for-byte. Coverage is explicit: a verifier that cannot apply to a world is reported "},{"id":"spn-41001","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-41002","text":", never counted as a pass or a fail. The Golden Spinner agrees 3/3; a bare Blank Spinner is a valid world for "},{"id":"spn-41003","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32"},{"id":"spn-41004","text":" but sits outside the Fixture oracle's domain. Exit codes: "},{"id":"spn-41005","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-41006","text":" agree, "},{"id":"spn-41007","marks":["code"],"text":"1"},{"id":"spn-41008","text":" ran-and-disagreed, "},{"id":"spn-41009","marks":["code"],"text":"2"},{"id":"spn-41010","text":" a verifier was unavailable. That makes any verifying command a fail-closed gate."}]},{"id":"blk-31131","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41011","text":"3. The environment surface (roadmap)"}]},{"id":"blk-31132","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41012","text":"The gap between \"a verifiable world\" and \"an environment an agent trains against\" is task/reward/episode lifecycle. The internal contract for that lifecycle is a "},{"id":"spn-41013","marks":["bold"],"text":"neutral Episode Kernel"},{"id":"spn-41014","text":" — public protocols are "},{"id":"spn-41015","marks":["italic"],"text":"adapters"},{"id":"spn-41016","text":" over it, never runtime law. This keeps "},{"id":"spn-41017","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://openreward.ai"}],"text":"Open Reward Standard"},{"id":"spn-41018","text":" or MCP evolution from ever becoming TRVM runtime semantics."}]},{"id":"blk-31133","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Episode Kernel   start · observe · step · reset · finalize   (internal, neutral)\n        ↓\nORS adapter      first / primary public surface  →  trvs serve --ors\nMCP adapter      compatibility (tools/resources/prompts)  →  trvs serve --mcp\nJSONL adapter    local automation / debugging"},{"id":"blk-31134","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41019","text":"The kernel carries "},{"id":"spn-41020","marks":["bold"],"text":"no substrate semantics"},{"id":"spn-41021","text":"; each verb is substrate-defined and may be declared "},{"id":"spn-41022","marks":["italic"],"text":"unsupported"},{"id":"spn-41023","text":" rather than faked. "},{"id":"spn-41024","marks":["code"],"text":"start"},{"id":"spn-41025","text":" prepares the frozen subject; "},{"id":"spn-41026","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize"},{"id":"spn-41027","text":" seals the trace and outputs, runs the verifier plan, scores the reward, and emits the episode. "},{"id":"spn-41028","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-41029","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-41030","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-41031","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-41032","marks":["code"],"text":"reset"},{"id":"spn-41033","text":" are supported only where a substrate can honour them — "},{"id":"spn-41034","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency v1 is one-shot and implements only `start → finalize`."},{"id":"spn-41035","text":" For the TRVM profile, "},{"id":"spn-41036","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-41037","text":" is a label-free "},{"id":"spn-41038","marks":["code"],"text":"_digest_domain"},{"id":"spn-41039","text":" projection, "},{"id":"spn-41040","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-41041","text":" extends the epoch-input stream, "},{"id":"spn-41042","marks":["code"],"text":"reset"},{"id":"spn-41043","text":" reconstructs "},{"id":"spn-41044","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-… + scen-…"},{"id":"spn-41045","text":" at epoch 0, and "},{"id":"spn-41046","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize"},{"id":"spn-41047","text":" checks "},{"id":"spn-41048","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32 == oracle"},{"id":"spn-41049","text":"; those are TRVM profile bindings, not kernel law. The ORS wire surface ("},{"id":"spn-41050","marks":["code"],"text":"list_tasks · session · call_tool → reward · finished"},{"id":"spn-41051","text":") and the MCP primitives ("},{"id":"spn-41052","marks":["code"],"text":"tools · resources · prompts"},{"id":"spn-41053","text":") are both "},{"id":"spn-41054","marks":["italic"],"text":"projections"},{"id":"spn-41055","text":" of the same kernel. The kernel owns the semantics; adapters only translate."}]},{"id":"blk-31135","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41056","text":"3a. The artifact ladder"}]},{"id":"blk-31136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41057","text":"TRAAVIIS freezes a "},{"id":"spn-41058","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate-neutral"},{"id":"spn-41059","text":" artifact ladder. The lowest rung is the "},{"id":"spn-41060","marks":["italic"],"text":"substrate subject"},{"id":"spn-41061","text":", sealed differently by each substrate; every rung above it is shared, so two researchers never argue about what agreed and what did not:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-31138","spans":[{"id":"spn-41062","text":"id / rung"}]},{"id":"blk-31139","spans":[{"id":"spn-41063","text":"question"}]},{"id":"blk-31140","spans":[{"id":"spn-41064","text":"domain"}]}],"id":"blk-31137","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-31141","spans":[{"id":"spn-41065","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate subject"}]},{"id":"blk-31142","spans":[{"id":"spn-41066","text":"was it the same subject?"}]},{"id":"blk-31143","spans":[{"id":"spn-41067","text":"TRVM: "},{"id":"spn-41068","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-41069","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-41070","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-41071","text":" · Residency: "},{"id":"spn-41072","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31144","spans":[{"id":"spn-41073","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"}]},{"id":"blk-31145","spans":[{"id":"spn-41074","text":"same scoring rubric?"}]},{"id":"blk-31146","spans":[{"id":"spn-41075","text":"declared reward spec"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31147","spans":[{"id":"spn-41076","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"}]},{"id":"blk-31148","spans":[{"id":"spn-41077","text":"same assignment?"}]},{"id":"blk-31149","spans":[{"id":"spn-41078","text":"subject + reward + terminate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31150","spans":[{"id":"spn-41079","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"}]},{"id":"blk-31151","spans":[{"id":"spn-41080","text":"same observable behavior?"}]},{"id":"blk-31152","spans":[{"id":"spn-41081","text":"the recorded observable record"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31153","spans":[{"id":"spn-41082","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"}]},{"id":"blk-31154","spans":[{"id":"spn-41083","text":"same evaluated outcome?"}]},{"id":"blk-31155","spans":[{"id":"spn-41084","text":"trace + rubric → receipt"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31156","spans":[{"id":"spn-41085","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"}]},{"id":"blk-31157","spans":[{"id":"spn-41086","text":"same environment release?"}]},{"id":"blk-31158","spans":[{"id":"spn-41087","text":"subject + tasks + rewards + splits"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31159","spans":[{"id":"spn-41088","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"}]},{"id":"blk-31160","spans":[{"id":"spn-41089","text":"same distributed package?"}]},{"id":"blk-31161","spans":[{"id":"spn-41090","text":"env + presentation + docs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-31162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41091","text":"The shared evaluation constructs ("},{"id":"spn-41092","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-41093","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41094","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-41095","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41096","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-41097","text":", the substrate profile) live in the "},{"id":"spn-41098","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.*"},{"id":"spn-41099","text":" namespace; substrate-specific evidence lives below. "},{"id":"spn-41100","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-41101","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41102","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-41103","text":" are "},{"id":"spn-41104","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM substrate identities"},{"id":"spn-41105","text":", not universal rungs; "},{"id":"spn-41106","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41107","text":" is the Residency subject. A "},{"id":"spn-41108","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trace-…`"},{"id":"spn-41109","text":" is the substrate-neutral observable record; a "},{"id":"spn-41110","marks":["bold"],"text":"`film-…`"},{"id":"spn-41111","text":" is the "},{"id":"spn-41112","marks":["italic"],"text":"TRVM case"},{"id":"spn-41113","text":" of a "},{"id":"spn-41114","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-41115","text":" — a deterministic-execution artifact that does not generalize. Forge owns TRVM compilation and identity ("},{"id":"spn-41116","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-41117","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41118","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-41119","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41120","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-41121","text":"); TRAAVIIS owns the shared evaluation ladder."}]},{"id":"blk-31163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41122","text":"Re-scoring the "},{"id":"spn-41123","marks":["italic"],"text":"same"},{"id":"spn-41124","text":" trace under a different rubric changes the "},{"id":"spn-41125","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-41126","text":" receipt but never the "},{"id":"spn-41127","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-41128","text":" — the recorded behavior did not change."}]},{"id":"blk-31164","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41129","text":"Canonical form (what an id is a hash "},{"id":"spn-41130","marks":["italic"],"text":"of"},{"id":"spn-41131","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-31165","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41132","text":"Every rung is "},{"id":"spn-41133","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-<sha256(canonical_bytes(document))>"},{"id":"spn-41134","text":", where "},{"id":"spn-41135","marks":["code"],"text":"canonical_bytes"},{"id":"spn-41136","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-41137","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS canonical JSON"},{"id":"spn-41138","text":": UTF-8, object keys sorted, no insignificant whitespace — concretely "},{"id":"spn-41139","marks":["code"],"text":"json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False)"},{"id":"spn-41140","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41141","text":"This is "},{"id":"spn-41142","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-41143","text":" RFC 8785 (JCS), and the difference is stated here rather than discovered by a reimplementer. It is byte-identical to RFC 8785 over documents whose keys hold no code point at or above U+10000 and whose numbers avoid four bands, but it differs in two ways that are already reachable:"}]},{"id":"blk-31167","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41144","marks":["bold"],"text":"Numbers."},{"id":"spn-41145","text":" RFC 8785 mandates ECMAScript "},{"id":"spn-41146","marks":["code"],"text":"Number::toString"},{"id":"spn-41147","text":"; Python does not"}]}],"id":"blk-31168","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41148","text":"match it for integral-valued floats below 10²¹ ("},{"id":"spn-41149","marks":["code"],"text":"1.0"},{"id":"spn-41150","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-41151","marks":["code"],"text":"1"},{"id":"spn-41152","text":"), for "},{"id":"spn-41153","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.0"},{"id":"spn-41154","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-41155","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.0"},{"id":"spn-41156","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-41157","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-41158","text":"), across "},{"id":"spn-41159","marks":["code"],"text":"[1e16, 1e21)"},{"id":"spn-41160","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-41161","marks":["code"],"text":"[1e-6, 1e-4)"},{"id":"spn-41162","text":", or on exponent zero-padding ("},{"id":"spn-41163","marks":["code"],"text":"1e-07"},{"id":"spn-41164","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-41165","marks":["code"],"text":"1e-7"},{"id":"spn-41166","text":"). A receipt's "},{"id":"spn-41167","marks":["code"],"text":"reward"},{"id":"spn-41168","text":" is always a float, so a fully-passing episode carries "},{"id":"spn-41169","marks":["code"],"text":"1.0"},{"id":"spn-41170","text":" and is on the diverging side."}]},{"id":"blk-31171","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41171","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key order."},{"id":"spn-41172","text":" RFC 8785 sorts property names by UTF-16 code unit; Python sorts"}]}],"id":"blk-31172","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41173","text":"by code point. These agree below U+10000 and diverge above it, so a subject repository containing an astral-plane filename orders its "},{"id":"spn-41174","marks":["code"],"text":"files"},{"id":"spn-41175","text":" map differently under the two schemes."}]},{"id":"blk-31175","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41176","text":"Nothing enforces the agreeing subset — there is no schema check, key charset check or numeric domain check anywhere on the path. "},{"id":"spn-41177","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_canonical.py"},{"id":"spn-41178","text":" measures all of this against a reference RFC 8785 implementation and pins each divergence with a reproducing value; treat it as the specification of the canonical form until a ruling decides whether to conform and migrate."}]},{"id":"blk-31176","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41179","text":"3b. The bundle — "},{"id":"spn-41180","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.environment.v1"}]},{"id":"blk-31177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41181","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-41182","text":" separates "},{"id":"spn-41183","marks":["italic"],"text":"what an environment means"},{"id":"spn-41184","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-41185","marks":["italic"],"text":"how it is shipped"},{"id":"spn-41186","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-41187","marks":["bold"],"text":"environment manifest"},{"id":"spn-41188","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-41189","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-41190","text":") fixes the substrate subject, tasks, rewards, action / observation or verifier profiles, and split membership; the outer "},{"id":"spn-41191","marks":["bold"],"text":"package"},{"id":"spn-41192","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-41193","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-41194","text":") carries presentation, docs, and screenshots and may change without moving "},{"id":"spn-41195","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-41196","text":". For the TRVM substrate it layers over the existing "},{"id":"spn-41197","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.bundle.v2"},{"id":"spn-41198","text":" (world + scenarios, already closed), adding "},{"id":"spn-41199","marks":["code"],"text":"{tasks, rewards, splits, profiles}"},{"id":"spn-41200","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41201","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-41202","text":" runs against a "},{"id":"spn-41203","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate-profile admission interface"},{"id":"spn-41204","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-41205","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_subject · verify_closure · recompute_subject_identity · reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-41206","text":"), not against "},{"id":"spn-41207","marks":["code"],"text":"world"},{"id":"spn-41208","text":" verbs; each substrate implements it (TRVM re-lowers source → "},{"id":"spn-41209","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-41210","text":"; Residency recomputes snapshot → "},{"id":"spn-41211","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41212","text":"). Three laws (mirroring the existing Forge bundle discipline):"}]},{"id":"blk-31179","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41213","marks":["bold"],"text":"self-sufficiency"},{"id":"spn-41214","text":" — the object set is derived from the doc."}]}],"id":"blk-31180","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41215","marks":["bold"],"text":"closure"},{"id":"spn-41216","text":" — the subject re-derives to its declared identity and every task /"}]}],"id":"blk-31182","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41217","text":"reward / subject reference resolves inside the closure, or import fails loudly."}]},{"id":"blk-31185","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41218","marks":["bold"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-41219","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-41220","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-41221","text":" re-opens and re-verifies the emitted bundle before"}]}],"id":"blk-31186","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41222","text":"reporting success."}]},{"id":"blk-31189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41223","marks":["bold"],"text":"Shipped"},{"id":"spn-41224","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-41225","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"},{"id":"spn-41226","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41227","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/pack.py"},{"id":"spn-41228","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41229","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/scaffold.py"},{"id":"spn-41230","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-41231","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-41232","text":" scaffolds and derives nothing — it emits scaffold-level references ("},{"id":"spn-41233","marks":["code"],"text":"reward_spec"},{"id":"spn-41234","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41235","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot_def"},{"id":"spn-41236","text":") precisely so it never asserts a hash it did not compute — and "},{"id":"spn-41237","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-41238","text":" replaces them with recomputed ids. "},{"id":"spn-41239","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-41240","text":" is derived from an explicit identity allowlist ("},{"id":"spn-41241","marks":["code"],"text":"substrate_profile · subject · tasks · rewards · profiles · splits"},{"id":"spn-41242","text":"), so renaming an environment or rewriting its description moves the "},{"id":"spn-41243","marks":["italic"],"text":"package"},{"id":"spn-41244","text":", never "},{"id":"spn-41245","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-41246","text":". Both substrate profiles are implemented; a single-task residency package is emitted as a runnable eval-bundle, closing "},{"id":"spn-41247","marks":["code"],"text":"init → pack → eval-one"},{"id":"spn-41248","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41249","text":"An episode emits a receipt:"}]},{"id":"blk-31191","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\", \"substrate_profile\": \"trvm.world.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\", \"subject\": { \"world\": \"sem-…\", \"scenario\": \"scen-…\" },\n  \"reward_id\": \"rew-…\", \"trace\": \"film-…\", \"episode_id\": \"episode-…\",\n  \"reward\": 1, \"status\": \"ok\", \"finished\": true,\n  \"verification\": { \"reference\": \"pass\", \"native\": \"pass\", \"oracle\": \"not_applicable\" } }"},{"id":"blk-31192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41250","text":"For a Residency episode the same receipt carries "},{"id":"spn-41251","marks":["code"],"text":"\"substrate_profile\": \"residency.repository.v1\""},{"id":"spn-41252","text":", a "},{"id":"spn-41253","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-41254","text":" in place of the "},{"id":"spn-41255","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-41256","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-41257","marks":["code"],"text":"citations"},{"id":"spn-41258","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41259","marks":["code"],"text":"patch"},{"id":"spn-41260","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41261","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"},{"id":"spn-41262","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41263","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-41264","text":" verifier fields. Every verifier field is one of "},{"id":"spn-41265","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"},{"id":"spn-41266","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41267","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41268","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41269","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-41270","text":", or "},{"id":"spn-41271","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41272","text":" — coverage is never silently dropped, and "},{"id":"spn-41273","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41274","text":" (substrate unavailable) stays distinct from "},{"id":"spn-41275","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41276","text":" (the work was wrong)."}]},{"id":"blk-31193","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41277","text":"3c. Evaluation before training"}]},{"id":"blk-31194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41278","text":"The first job is not a trainer, and the first interface is not a batch. It is a one-shot "},{"id":"spn-41279","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvs eval-one task.json --agent-command …`"},{"id":"spn-41280","text":" over a single frozen subject. Batch "},{"id":"spn-41281","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-41282","text":" follows once eval-one is boring. Because every episode is verified and content-addressed, the numbers are reproducible and the traces are re-checkable. Training frameworks drive rollouts "},{"id":"spn-41283","marks":["italic"],"text":"through"},{"id":"spn-41284","text":" the ORS adapter later."}]},{"id":"blk-31195","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41285","marks":["bold"],"text":"Shipped"},{"id":"spn-41286","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-41287","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/evalsplit.py"},{"id":"spn-41288","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-41289","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval PKG --split NAME"},{"id":"spn-41290","text":" runs an agent over a split and emits one "},{"id":"spn-41291","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-41292","text":" per task. It adds "},{"id":"spn-41293","marks":["bold"],"text":"no rung to the ladder"},{"id":"spn-41294","text":" — §1 stops at "},{"id":"spn-41295","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-41296","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41297","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-41298","text":", so a run over a split gets an "},{"id":"spn-41299","marks":["italic"],"text":"index"},{"id":"spn-41300","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-41301","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.evaluation.v1"},{"id":"spn-41302","text":") naming the "},{"id":"spn-41303","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-41304","text":", the split, and the episode ids, and carries no id of its own. The admission order mirrors "},{"id":"spn-41305","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-41306","text":": reopen the package (every id re-derived from the written bytes) → resolve the split → bind the subject tree to its snapshot → "},{"id":"spn-41307","marks":["italic"],"text":"only then"},{"id":"spn-41308","text":" launch anything. A task that fails is recorded as a failed episode and the split continues; a refusal exits 2 rather than reporting a score of zero."}]},{"id":"blk-31196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41309","marks":["italic"],"text":"Canonical form."},{"id":"spn-41310","text":" An environment is a closed "},{"id":"spn-41311","marks":["bold"],"text":"set"},{"id":"spn-41312","text":" of tasks, rewards and split members (§3), and a set has exactly one written order — so "},{"id":"spn-41313","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-41314","text":" sorts tasks and rewards by their derived ids and split members by task id, and reordering an author's source list moves no identity. Producing that order is not enough: "},{"id":"spn-41315","marks":["code"],"text":"open_package"},{"id":"spn-41316","text":" "},{"id":"spn-41317","marks":["bold"],"text":"re-checks"},{"id":"spn-41318","text":" it, because a hand-built manifest that is internally consistent but unsorted would otherwise reopen cleanly and give one environment as many identities as its task list has permutations. A noncanonical manifest is "},{"id":"spn-41319","marks":["code"],"text":"MANIFEST_NONCANONICAL"},{"id":"spn-41320","text":", checked before the "},{"id":"spn-41321","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-41322","text":" comparison so the failure reads as a malformed "},{"id":"spn-41323","marks":["italic"],"text":"form"},{"id":"spn-41324","text":" rather than a confusing identity mismatch."}]},{"id":"blk-31197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41325","marks":["italic"],"text":"Two outcomes, not one."},{"id":"spn-41326","text":" Each index entry carries "},{"id":"spn-41327","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-41328","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41329","marks":["code"],"text":"reward"},{"id":"spn-41330","text":" — what the evaluation found — and a separate "},{"id":"spn-41331","marks":["code"],"text":"persistence {requested, status, error}"},{"id":"spn-41332","text":" — whether the evidence the caller asked to keep was kept. Conflating them once let a run report "},{"id":"spn-41333","marks":["code"],"text":"ok"},{"id":"spn-41334","text":" for an episode whose bundle had failed to write: a score with no retained proof, reported as if the proof existed. The totals count both, and the exit code reads them in precedence — persistence failure 2, disagreement 1, otherwise 0. "},{"id":"spn-41335","marks":["code"],"text":"OSError"},{"id":"spn-41336","text":" is caught alongside "},{"id":"spn-41337","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeBundleError"},{"id":"spn-41338","text":" deliberately: a read-only output directory is the most ordinary way retention fails, and it must be a recorded outcome for one task rather than an exception that abandons the rest of the split."}]},{"id":"blk-31198","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41339","text":"3c-bis. Verifier wiring — "},{"id":"spn-41340","marks":["code"],"text":"VerifierRegistryV1"}]},{"id":"blk-31199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41341","text":"Three things that are easy to conflate are kept distinct:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-31201","spans":[{"id":"spn-41342","text":"layer"}]},{"id":"blk-31202","spans":[{"id":"spn-41343","text":"function of"}]},{"id":"blk-31203","spans":[{"id":"spn-41344","text":"where it lives"}]}],"id":"blk-31200","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-31204","spans":[{"id":"spn-41345","text":"declared plan"}]},{"id":"blk-31205","spans":[{"id":"spn-41346","text":"the task alone"}]},{"id":"blk-31206","spans":[{"id":"spn-41347","marks":["code"],"text":"wiring.declared_signals"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31207","spans":[{"id":"spn-41348","text":"available implementations"}]},{"id":"blk-31208","spans":[{"id":"spn-41349","text":"task + runtime/registry"}]},{"id":"blk-31209","spans":[{"id":"spn-41350","marks":["code"],"text":"VerifierRegistryV1"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31210","spans":[{"id":"spn-41351","text":"sealed history"}]},{"id":"blk-31211","spans":[{"id":"spn-41352","text":"what actually answered"}]},{"id":"blk-31212","spans":[{"id":"spn-41353","marks":["code"],"text":"receipt.verifier_versions"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-31213","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41354","text":"The registry is built "},{"id":"spn-41355","marks":["bold"],"text":"once per command"},{"id":"spn-41356","text":" from the engine that command selected, so every task in a split is answered by the same verifiers bound to the same Forge checkout — and "},{"id":"spn-41357","marks":["code"],"text":"real_adapter(forge_api)"},{"id":"spn-41358","text":" takes that engine explicitly rather than independently rediscovering a possibly different one. An unreachable engine leaves "},{"id":"spn-41359","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-41360","text":" declared but unwired, reported as a note; it is never silently dropped and never faked into a "},{"id":"spn-41361","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"},{"id":"spn-41362","text":". Because the versions are sealed into "},{"id":"spn-41363","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-41364","text":", an engine upgrade honestly moves the episode id instead of quietly re-scoring the same one."}]},{"id":"blk-31214","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41365","text":"3c-ter. Test plans — "},{"id":"spn-41366","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.test-plan.v2"}]},{"id":"blk-31215","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41367","text":"V2 replaced host-specific "},{"id":"spn-41368","marks":["code"],"text":"argv"},{"id":"spn-41369","text":" with a logical "},{"id":"spn-41370","marks":["code"],"text":"tool"},{"id":"spn-41371","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-41372","marks":["code"],"text":"args"},{"id":"spn-41373","text":" under a named "},{"id":"spn-41374","marks":["code"],"text":"toolchain_profile"},{"id":"spn-41375","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-41376","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-41377","text":" is host-independent and the resolved binary is an execution fact. It further lets each command declare per-phase "},{"id":"spn-41378","marks":["code"],"text":"allowed_exit_codes"},{"id":"spn-41379","text":", both defaulting to "},{"id":"spn-41380","marks":["code"],"text":"[0]"},{"id":"spn-41381","text":" — exactly the V1 rule, so an undeclared plan keeps its old meaning. This is what makes a "},{"id":"spn-41382","marks":["bold"],"text":"repair task"},{"id":"spn-41383","text":" expressible: under a hardcoded baseline-must-exit-0 rule, a task could not require a test that fails before the fix and passes after, which is the ordinary shape of a real bug report. The verdict asymmetry is deliberate — the baseline judges the "},{"id":"spn-41384","marks":["italic"],"text":"fixture"},{"id":"spn-41385","text":" (a miss is "},{"id":"spn-41386","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41387","text":", the task is inadmissible), the patched run judges the "},{"id":"spn-41388","marks":["italic"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-41389","text":" (a miss is "},{"id":"spn-41390","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41391","text":") — and every record states the "},{"id":"spn-41392","marks":["code"],"text":"expected_exit_codes"},{"id":"spn-41393","text":" it was judged by, so the evidence names its own rule."}]},{"id":"blk-31216","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41394","text":"3d. Later: verified process rewards"}]},{"id":"blk-31217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41395","text":"Because TRVM films observe each transition, TRAAVIIS can eventually emit intermediate, verifier-grounded rewards (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-41396","marks":["code"],"text":"+0.2 preserved safety invariant"},{"id":"spn-41397","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41398","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.3 duplicated forbidden resource"},{"id":"spn-41399","text":") rather than only a terminal reward. This depends entirely on verifier reliability, so it ships "},{"id":"spn-41400","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-41401","text":" deterministic terminal rewards and complete episodes are solid."}]},{"id":"blk-31218","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41402","text":"4. Sequencing"}]},{"id":"blk-31219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41403","text":"The thesis is "},{"id":"spn-41404","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade environments for evaluating agents"},{"id":"spn-41405","text":". The sequencing builds "},{"id":"spn-41406","marks":["italic"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-41407","text":" end-to-end evaluation environment before widening the platform. Flagship worlds ship in this order:"}]},{"id":"blk-31220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41408","marks":["bold"],"text":"Golden Spinner → Evidence Residency → Courier → WallRider."}]},{"id":"blk-31221","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41409","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.7-5 (Spinner Bench)"},{"id":"spn-41410","text":" — close the Public Alpha: freeze presentation,"}]}],"id":"blk-31222","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41411","text":"package source, document limits, publish reproducible acceptance. Then freeze Bench feature work. Bench proceeds "},{"id":"spn-41412","marks":["italic"],"text":"independently"},{"id":"spn-41413","text":" and does not block the evaluation surface below."}]},{"id":"blk-31225","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41414","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.1"},{"id":"spn-41415","text":" — the shared artifact ladder as pure identity functions"}]}],"id":"blk-31226","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41416","text":"("},{"id":"spn-41417","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot_id · finding_id · patch_id · trace_id · reward_id · task_id · episode_id"},{"id":"spn-41418","text":") with mutation-law tests, then "},{"id":"spn-41419","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-41420","text":" over "},{"id":"spn-41421","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency"},{"id":"spn-41422","text":" — an agent inspects a frozen repository, finds a real spec/impl inconsistency, cites evidence, proposes the smallest patch, runs the declared checks, and returns a structured finding + a re-verifiable receipt. Ship Golden Spinner as the first TRVM bundle alongside. See "},{"id":"spn-41423","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_EVIDENCE_RESIDENCY.md"},{"id":"spn-41424","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31229","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41425","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.2"},{"id":"spn-41426","text":" — the Episode Kernel + "},{"id":"spn-41427","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors"},{"id":"spn-41428","text":"; ship the"}]}],"id":"blk-31230","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31232","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41429","marks":["bold"],"text":"Courier"},{"id":"spn-41430","text":"/Factory world so the kernel is exercised by a stateful, long-horizon environment "},{"id":"spn-41431","marks":["italic"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-41432","text":" batch "},{"id":"spn-41433","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-41434","text":" is called complete."}]},{"id":"blk-31233","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41435","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.3"},{"id":"spn-41436","text":" — batch "},{"id":"spn-41437","marks":["code"],"text":"eval · compare · reports"},{"id":"spn-41438","text":" over the kernel; MCP"}]}],"id":"blk-31234","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41439","text":"adapter."}]},{"id":"blk-31237","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31239","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41440","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.4"},{"id":"spn-41441","text":" — an ORS/TRL example, process-reward hooks, environment"}]}],"id":"blk-31238","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41442","text":"publishing; ship the "},{"id":"spn-41443","marks":["bold"],"text":"WallRider"},{"id":"spn-41444","text":"/Graffiti world."}]},{"id":"blk-31241","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41445","text":"5. What is deliberately not built"}]},{"id":"blk-31242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41446","text":"Model routing · generic sub-agent orchestration · another chat interface · a cloud GPU training service · a giant environment marketplace · a complete game engine · plugin systems before the bundle/session API is stable · a complex interactive REPL · automatic LLM world generation as the core proposition."}]},{"id":"blk-31243","kind":"parag